From f36bb5c63ca1cb602584c18671cc59e0e4eaee48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
Date: Sat, 15 Nov 2025 12:21:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fortran: Finalize function results per ISO F2018 7.5.6.3

ISO/IEC 1539-1:2018 requires finalizing derived-function results after
intrinsic assignment.  Ensure user-defined assignments defer RHS cleanup
until after the call, keep constructor finalization tied to
GFC_STD_F2018_DEL, and add a regression test demonstrating the behavior.

	PR fortran/121472

gcc/fortran/ChangeLog:

	* resolve.cc (resolve_ordinary_assign): Mark RHS function results in
	user-defined assignments for deferred finalization.
	* trans.cc (gfc_derived_needs_copy, gfc_finalize_tree_expr): Guard
	CALL_EXPR finalization behind actual allocatable components to avoid
	superfluous deep copies.
	* trans-expr.cc (gfc_conv_procedure_call): Evaluate and defer
	finalization of derived RHS function actuals, dereferencing temporaries
	before cleanup; keep constructor finalization suppression under
	gfc_notification_std (GFC_STD_F2018_DEL).

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gfortran.dg/finalize_45.f90: Update comment to reflect ISO behavior.
	* gfortran.dg/finalize_constructor_1.f90: New test covering constructor
	interfaces plus finalizers.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
---
